# Dynamic Workflow Using RFile (Recommended)

If your lead says **don't hardcode the Age Group**, use the **RFile**.

### Step 1

Input

```
TFile
```

### Step 2

Calculate

```
Age
```

### Step 3

Input

```
RFile
```

It contains

| Age | Age Group |
| --- | --------- |
| 1   | 1-7       |
| 8   | 8-30      |
| 31  | 31-60     |
| 61  | 61-90     |
| 91  | 91-180    |
| 181 | 181-365   |
| 366 | >365      |

---

### Step 4

Use **Append Fields**

Connect

```
TFile
```

to Target

Connect

```
RFile
```

to Source

Every transaction now gets all age ranges.

Suppose

```
Age = 48
```

It becomes

| Age | RFile Age |
| --- | --------- |
| 48  | 1         |
| 48  | 8         |
| 48  | 31        |
| 48  | 61        |
| 48  | 91        |
| 48  | 181       |
| 48  | 366       |

---

### Step 5

Add a **Filter Tool**

Condition

```alteryx
[Age] >= [RFile Age]
```

Now

```
48
```

keeps

```
1
8
31
```

---

### Step 6

Add a **Sort Tool**

Sort by

```
RFile Age
```

Descending

Result

```
31
8
1
```

---

### Step 7

Add a **Sample Tool**

Choose

```
First 1 Row
```

Now only

```
31
```

remains.

Age Group becomes

```
31-60
```

---

### Step 8

Join back with TFile (if required) or continue the flow to add the remaining columns and output to YFile.

---

# Recommended Complete Workflow

```
TFile
   │
Input Data
   │
Select
   │
Formula (Age)
   │
Append Fields
   │
RFile
   │
Filter (Age >= RFile Age)
   │
Sort (RFile Age Desc)
   │
Sample (First 1)
   │
Formula (Group Owner, Owner)
   │
Select (Column Mapping)
   │
Output Data (YFile)
```

This **dynamic workflow** is considered a best practice because if the age ranges in the RFile change (for example, adding `366–730` or modifying ranges), you only need to update the RFile—no changes to the Alteryx formulas are required.
